SYNTHETIC DATA — NOT real SALT data.
================================================================================

Everything in this directory is SYNTHETIC, generated deterministically by
`scripts/generate_salt_synthetic.py`. It contains NO real records from SAP's SALT
dataset.

Why synthetic: the real SALT dataset is access-gated on Hugging Face, and
redistributing a derived sample of a gated dataset is legally and ethically
unclear — and would break this repository's clone-and-run guarantee. So we
instead generate our own data using SALT's *schema* as the reference.

Schema reference (credit):
  SALT — Sales Autocompletion Linked Business Tables (SAP AI Research)
  Paper:   arXiv:2501.03413
  Dataset: https://huggingface.co/datasets/SAP/SALT   (gated)

This synthetic dataset reproduces SALT's table names, columns, and join keys
(I_Customer, I_AddrOrgNamePostalAddress linked by AddressID; I_SalesDocument and
I_SalesDocumentItem linked by SalesDocument; sales documents reference customers
via the SoldToParty / ShipToParty / BillToParty / PayerParty roles). Because the
ingester is written against this real schema, ingesting the *actual* SALT dataset
is a documented drop-in — gated only by Hugging Face access — needing no change
to the ingester, engine, or tests.

License: this synthetic data is part of the Tessera project and is provided under
the project's MIT license (see ../../LICENSE). It carries NO CC-BY-NC-SA
encumbrance, because it contains no SALT data. The SALT license applies only to
the real SALT dataset, which is not redistributed here.
